zerbaijan should build  security should undertake measures to  reduce tensions on the borders but it's  azerbaijan who is refusing to implement  these trilateral statement okay so just  to  clarify again so when the azeri said  that armenia had agreed to pull back its  troops from the border this is not what  you agreed as far as you're concerned  mean this is uh i mean it's ridiculous  uh no any state would withdraw its  troops from southern territory i mean i  don't know  what is the  misperception around this issue that  armenia should withdraw its troops from  its borders but  armenia is a sovereign country it's a  member of united states  it's a member of united nations and thus  armenia has all rights for self-defense  okay now francis said it wants to raise  this latest escalation to uh the u.n  security council do you support the  european union's role here in this  dispute  i mean we are looking forward to  cooperate with all those who can  contribute uh towards peace in our  region  and uh of course  uh we understand that  uh  there are certain  countries organizations which offer  their good offices and of course we are  using those  good offices in order  to  to come to the peace to our region  can you tell us sir about the status of  the russian peacekeepers uh who were at  the border who were supposed to be  keeping the peace there what is their  current status  i mean let's uh  just uh there is i think we need uh uh  to  to clarify one thing russian  peacekeepers they are in  nagorno-karabakh sure and  they are  uh they are not on the border between  armenia and azerbaijan they are on  nagorno-karabakh and they play key role  in  ensuring  security for the people of nagorno-kara  and they are deployed there by the  trilateral  statement of november  9 2020  so the the areas where the fighting has  been happening in the last few hours  tell us a bit more about their  significance to your country  first of all it should be established  that the the situation remains very  tense  and hostilities are not stopped  elsewhere  they are still ongoing hostilities in  different sections of the border  and  this  and as i said  azerbaijan not merely  not nearly a violated ceasefire  across border but it also targeted  armenian positions and also civilian  infrastructures inside armenia  so it's a clear attack on sovereign  country its clear attack on u.n member  state  thank you very much for taking the time  to speak to us vahe gargovian armenia's  deputy foreign minister joining us there  from yerevan thank you
 

